o is used if not set)", "pattern_descriptor": "YYYY-MM-DD"}, "credentials": {"type": "object", "order": 0, "title": "Google Credentials", "required": ["developer_token", "client_id", "client_secret", "refresh_token"], "properties": {"client_id": {"type": "string", "order": 1, "title": "Client ID", "description": "The Client ID of your Google Ads developer application. For detailed instructions on finding this value, refer to our <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/google-ads#setup-guide\\">documentation</a>."}, "access_token": {"type": "string", "order": 4, "title": "Access Token", "description": "The Access Token for making authenticated requests. For detailed instructions on finding this value, refer to our <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/google-ads#setup-guide\\">documentation</a>.", "airbyte_secret": true}, "client_secret":{"_secret":"REDACTED"}, "refresh_token": {"type": "string", "order": 3, "title": "Refresh Token", "description": "The token used to obtain a new Access Token. For detailed instructions on finding this value, refer to our <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/google-ads#setup-guide\\">documentation</a>.", "airbyte_secret": true}, "developer_token": {"type": "string", "order": 0, "title": "Developer Token", "description": "The Developer Token granted by Google to use their APIs. For detailed instructions on finding this value, refer to our <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/google-ads#setup-guide\\">documentation</a>.", "airbyte_secret": true}}, "description": ""}, "customer_id": {"type": "string", "order": 1, "title": "Customer ID(s)", "pattern": "^[0-9]{10}(,[0-9]{10})*$", "examples": ["6783948572,5839201945"], "description": "Comma-separated list of (client) customer IDs. Each customer ID must be specified as a 10-digit number without dashes. For detailed instructions on finding this value, refer to our <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/google-ads#setup-guide\\">documentation</a>.", "pattern_descriptor": "The customer ID must be 10 digits. Separate multiple customer IDs using commas."}, "custom_queries_array": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["query", "table_name"], "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "title": "Custom Query", "examples": ["SELECT segments.ad_destination_type, campaign.advertising_channel_sub_type FROM campaign WHERE campaign.status = 'PAUSED'"], "multiline": true, "description": "A custom defined GAQL query for building the report. Avoid including the segments.date field; wherever possible, Airbyte will automatically include it for incremental syncs. For more information, refer to <a href=\\"https://developers.google.com/google-ads/api/fields/v11/overview_query_builder\\">Google's documentation</a>."}, "table_name": {"type": "string", "title": "Destination Table Name", "description": "The table name in your destination database for the chosen query."}}}, "order": 5, "title": "Custom GAQL Queries", "description": ""}, "conversion_window_days": {"type": "integer", "order": 6, "title": "Conversion Window", "default": 14, "maximum": 1095, "minimum": 0, "examples": [14], "description": "A conversion window is the number of days after an ad interaction (such as an ad click or video view) during which a conversion, such as a purchase, is recorded in Google Ads. For more information, see <a href=\\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/3123169?hl=en\\">Google's documentation</a>."}, "customer_status_filter": {"type": "array", "items": {"enum": ["UNKNOWN", "ENABLED", "CANCELED", "SUSPENDED", "CLOSED"], "title": "CustomerStatus", "description": "An enumeration."}, "order": 2, "title": "Customer Statuses Filter", "default": [], "description": "A list of customer statuses to filter on. For detailed info about what each status mean refer to Google Ads <a href=\\"https://developers.google.com/google-ads/api/reference/rpc/v15/CustomerStatusEnum.CustomerS