r the access ID. It is a 40-character base-64 encoded string.", "airbyte_secret": true}, "hmac_key_access_id": {"type": "string", "order": 1, "title": "HMAC Key Access ID", "examples": ["1234567890abcdefghij1234"], "description": "HMAC key access ID. When linked to a service account, this ID is 61 characters long; when linked to a user account, it is 24 characters long.", "airbyte_secret": true}}}], "order": 1, "title": "Credential", "description": "An HMAC key is a type of credential and can be associated with a service account or a user account in Cloud Storage. Read more <a href=\\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/authentication/hmackeys\\">here</a>."}, "gcs_bucket_name": {"type": "string", "order": 2, "title": "GCS Bucket Name", "examples": ["airbyte_sync"], "description": "The name of the GCS bucket. Read more <a href=\\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/naming-buckets\\">here</a>."}, "gcs_bucket_path": {"type": "string", "order": 3, "title": "GCS Bucket Path", "examples": ["data_sync/test"], "description": "Directory under the GCS bucket where data will be written."}, "keep_files_in_gcs-bucket": {"enum": ["Delete all tmp files from GCS", "Keep all tmp files in GCS"], "type": "string", "order": 4, "title": "GCS Tmp Files Afterward Processing", "default": "Delete all tmp files from GCS", "description": "This upload method is supposed to temporary store records in GCS bucket. By this select you can chose if these records should be removed from GCS when migration has finished. The default \\"Delete all tmp files from GCS\\" value is used if not set explicitly."}}, "description": "<i>(recommended)</i> Writes large batches of records to a file, uploads the file to GCS, then uses COPY INTO to load your data into BigQuery. Provides best-in-class speed, reliability and scalability. Read more about GCS Staging <a href=\\"https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/destinations/bigquery#gcs-staging\\">here</a>."}, {"title": "Standard Inserts", "required": ["method"], 